    - motion: Brisk Walk
      note: 'The brisk walk is also shown past the speed its strides are made for, up to this many times it (Multiply), played up to this many times faster (Time Scale): so it quickens a little and its planted feet slide a little (it reaches further than it''s sped up). Few people walk much faster than a brisk walk (they break into a run), so a walk past it must hurry or slide; this keeps both small. The run takes over past it. Both are shares of the clip''s own speed, so they hold whatever it''s measured at.'
      threshold:
        kind: 1
        constant: 0
        clip: Brisk Walk
        direction: {x: 0, y: 0}
        multiply: 1.5
        reciprocal: 0
